  "description": "Register, sign in and sign out as JSON endpoints, for an ASP.NET Core app that renders no Rask components — a TypeScript SPA host or a meta-framework host, where the front end owns the UI. Accounts are backed by ASP.NET Core Identity (versioned password hashing, lockout, security stamps) and exposed at /api/auth, with email confirmation and password reset through the app's own mail queue and optional bearer tokens. The first account to register becomes the admin. This is the host-neutral half of Rask.Auth: no components, no renderer, no Rask.Core. Add Rask.Auth instead when the app IS a Rask app and wants the built-in sign-in pages.",
